{"chars": "Here is why. Orchids are one of the biggest families of flowers in the world, and they grow almost everywhere: in steamy jungles and on windy mountaintops, in deserts and in swamps, on every continent except icy Antarctica. Some brave little orchids even grow far, far north on the Arctic tundra. But the North Pole itself isn't land at all. It is frozen ocean, a giant floating sheet of sea ice with no soil anywhere. Nothing grows there by itself. No trees, no grass, and not a single orchid.", "start": [0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.45, 0.45, 0.45, 0.6, 0.6, 0.6, 0.6, 1.15, 1.312, 1.312, 1.312, 1.312, 1.312, 1.312, 1.312, 1.312, 1.85, 1.85, 1.85, 1.85, 1.95, 1.95, 1.95, 1.95, 2.087, 2.087, 2.087, 2.163, 2.163, 2.163, 2.163, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.625, 2.625, 2.625, 2.625, 2.625, 2.625, 2.625, 2.625, 2.625, 3.087, 3.087, 3.087, 3.188, 3.188, 3.188, 3.188, 3.188, 3.188, 3.188, 3.188, 3.638, 3.638, 3.638, 3.712, 3.712, 3.712, 3.712, 3.8, 3.8, 3.8, 3.8, 3.8, 3.8, 4.425, 4.525, 4.525, 4.525, 4.525, 4.638, 4.638, 4.638, 4.638, 4.638, 4.775, 4.775, 4.775, 4.775, 4.775, 5.075, 5.075, 5.075, 5.075, 5.075, 5.075, 5.075, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 5.475, 6.225, 6.325, 6.325, 6.325, 6.475, 6.475, 6.475, 6.475, 6.475, 6.475, 6.475, 6.862, 6.862, 6.862, 6.862, 6.862, 6.862, 6.862, 6.862, 7.375, 7.375, 7.375, 7.375, 7.487, 7.487, 7.487, 7.625, 7.625, 7.625, 7.625, 7.625, 7.625, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 7.925, 8.775, 8.85, 8.85, 8.85, 9.0, 9.0, 9.0, 9.0, 9.0, 9.0, 9.0, 9.0, 9.425, 9.425, 9.425, 9.425, 9.55, 9.55, 9.55, 9.713, 9.713, 9.713, 9.713, 9.713, 9.713, 9.713, 10.375, 10.475, 10.475, 10.475, 10.625, 10.625, 10.625, 10.625, 10.625, 10.625, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 10.925, 11.425, 11.425, 11.425, 11.425, 11.425, 11.425, 11.425, 11.838, 11.838, 11.838, 11.838, 12.175, 12.175, 12.175, 12.175, 